<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RMB Holdings yr shr, div surges.</title>
<headline>RMB Holdings yr shr, div surges.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   219.3	 vs 156.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 90.0	  vs 64.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   161.1	 vs 114.8</p>
<p>    Income after tax	148.1	 vs 105.1</p>
<p>    Outside shareholders' 44.7	  vs 32.8</p>
<p>Div payable October 31</p>
<p>on register October 18</p>
<p>Full name: RMB Holdings Ltd (banking)</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  59.2	  vs 43.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the group's operating subsidiaries and associates were seen achieving their targetted growths for the year which would in turn enable RMB to achieve its target of 20 percent growth per annum.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
